# Multi-tenant membership

A SaaS user belongs to organizations through `Membership`. One user, many orgs. Role lives on the membership. `Session` is identity only (this browser is this user). The current tenant is a signed `organization_id` cookie, checked against a membership row.

```ruby
# bad
class User
  belongs_to :organization
  enum :role, { operator: "operator", admin: "admin" }
end

class Session
  belongs_to :user
  belongs_to :organization
end

Current.organization = Current.session.organization
```

```ruby
# good
class Membership
  belongs_to :user
  belongs_to :organization
  enum :role, { operator: "operator", admin: "admin" }
end

class Session
  belongs_to :user
end

membership = user.memberships.find_by!(organization_id: cookies.signed[:organization_id])
Current.organization = membership.organization
```

Do not put `organization_id` or `role` on `users`. Do not put `organization_id` on `sessions`. Destroying an org destroys memberships, not users. Coverage is membership outcomes, org isolation, and controller 404s when the actor is outside the tenant.
